## Lore

The New German Republic''s covert specialist, working in sabotage, surveillance, impersonation, robbery, assassination, rescue, prison breaks and every other kind of covert operation. The officer''s services are used by both the intelligence division and the civilian law enforcement branch of the military.

Alignment: Any.

## Rank and pay

Standard military, but as an officer even a first level character starts at the rank of lieutenant. Salary is 2500 credits a month, rising to 4500 to 8000 for eighth level and higher, with a private two bedroom apartment.

## Cybernetics

A gyro-compass, clock calendar, universal headjack, and ear with amplified hearing and a toxic filter, all standard to start. Officers of eighth level or higher are likely to add one or two cybernetic eyes, a lung implant, a cyber-disguise type AA-1, a cybernetic finger or two, or an artificial arm. Others may be purchased, awarded for heroism, or provided for a mission.

## GM Notes

Issued alongside the stored equipment, and not given catalog rows: an energy rifle of choice, a sidearm of choice and a vibro-blade of choice, all unresolved choices; two plasma grenades, which the catalog has no row for; and T-11 Enhanced body armour and the T-100 Eagle jet pack, which are vessel-shaped stat blocks this catalog does not hold.

Available on assignment: additional body armour, weapons, equipment, surveillance and recording gear, cameras, computers and sensory equipment, plus access to the T-Series power armour, X-Series robots, the EIR-15 gargoyle bot and other transport. Access to most military bases at high to highest security clearance, and always priority over surveillance and communications equipment, explosives, cybernetics, EIRs and weapons.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ngr-intelligence-officer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ngr-intelligence-officer';

